=== (a) A DEFECT IN MY OWN SPEC. The overlap rule was written for the wrong detector.
============================================================================================================================
    rank correlation( D1_DIR_EFF   , PATH_EFF_TRANS score ) = +0.229
    rank correlation( D3_RANGE_EXP , PATH_EFF_TRANS score ) = +0.968

    PATH_EFF_TRANS = (1 - path efficiency) x (range / trailing mean range).
    D3_RANGE_EXP   =                          range / trailing mean range.
    D3 IS A MULTIPLICATIVE FACTOR INSIDE THE HELD-OUT ENGINE'S OWN SCORE. That is a
    strictly worse overlap than the D1 case the spec disclosed, and by the spec's own
    logic the same discount must apply. The clean holdout is VALUE_REACCEPT alone.

    CLEAN HOLDOUT (VALUE_REACCEPT only), D3_RANGE_EXP @ 0.50:
        real delta $81/trade   random-veto null mean $-3 p95 $170  -> 82.0th percentile   FAILS
    The wave's verdict does not change - the primary already failed at the 85th
    percentile. This makes the failure cleaner, it does not rescue anything.

